  "question": {
    "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>25</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mL</mi></math> of silver nitrate solution <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mo>)</mo></math> is added dropwise to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>25</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mL</mi></math> of potassium iodide <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>05</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mo>)</mo></math> solution. The ion(s) present in very small quantity in the solution is/are",
    "image": null
  },
